cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SENECA, please cite the original article (preferred-citation).
  If it matters which program produced your results, please also cite this
  port with its version.
type: software
title: "SENECA (2001 JCICS version, modern port)"
abstract: >-
  A faithful port of SENECA, the program for computer-assisted structure
  elucidation (CASE) of organic compounds published in 2001, to Java 25 and
  the Chemistry Development Kit (CDK) 2.13, with a Swing user interface
  packaged as a macOS application. SENECA searches the constitutional isomers
  of a molecular formula by simulated annealing and scores each candidate
  structure against NMR data with a set of judges. The port reproduces the
  results of the 2001 program, checked against a golden master recorded with
  the original code; every deviation is documented.
